notes/finesser/.out/

# Per-machine agent/editor config — local to whoever's clone this is.
.claude/

# Design mocks — high-res Figma exports (~107MB) used only as build reference.
# Kept LOCAL: they sit inside the Netlify publish dir, so committing them would
# deploy 107MB to the public CDN and bloat the repo. Each chat's clone gets its
# own copy from Sean; they are build INPUT, not source.
website/mocks/

# ── The "Coming Soon" splash build (2026-06) ────────────────────────────────
# A separate, finished piece of work: the Oxygen splash page, assembled from
# Figma frames. It has nothing to do with the section/fragment site under
# website/ — different assets, different namespace (.brg-cs), different target.
# It was never committed, and it shouldn't be: ~60MB of source SVG, fonts and
# photography for a page that is about to be retired at launch, sitting at the
# repo ROOT where a stray `git add -A` would sweep it in.
#
# It is still on disk in this clone. If it ever needs to be versioned it wants
# its own repo, not this one.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ROOT-ANCHORED (leading /) ON PURPOSE. A bare `assets/`
# would also match `website/assets/` — gitignore matches at any depth — and
# would then silently swallow every new file Finn adds to the real asset dir.
/index.html
/blocks.html
/build.py
/README-splash.md
/OXYGEN-BUILD-GUIDE.md
/OXYGEN-IMPLEMENTATION.md
/assets/
/css/
/components/
/splash/
/oxygen/
/new-project-starter/
/brg-coming-soon-package*/
/brg-coming-soon-package*.zip
